                <pb facs="1150" n="1140" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1140"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.801/9–3049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Holmes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-30T11:00:00+01:00">September 30,
                            1949—11 a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 30—5:50 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3925. Deptel 3545, September 29. According FonOff, British Embassy, Washington,
                    did ask for text British protest re <hi rendition="#italic">Edith Moller</hi>
                    but did not mention use of telegraph. Had planned forward text by pouch but view
                    urgency will telegraph this morning priority basis. Comments document may not be
                    too helpful as it is “indignant” rather than “legal” in tone. Declined Embassy
                    offer cable text.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Holmes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
